# GNU tests/cp disposition (66 scripts). Every script has a verdict;
# the mined runner asserts this file covers exactly the corpus
# (sprint 08D). Columns: <script> <verdict> <reason>
#
# Verdicts:
#   mined      runs against chopin unmodified and passes (or defers to
#              a documented register deviation)
#   skip-root  needs privileges; the harness refuses root
#   skip-sel   needs an SELinux-enabled kernel (build-parity: chopin
#              and the pinned oracle are both non-SELinux)
#   skip-acl   needs setfacl/getfacl (build-parity: ACL-disabled
#              oracle; cp-visible ACL-xattr travel is golden-covered)
#   skip-mv    exercises mv, excluded from cp v0.1 (non-goal)
#   skip-fs    needs a second filesystem / special mount (runs on the
#              fs-job lane where CHOPIN_TEST_FSROOT is set)
#   skip-env   needs a tool absent by default (valgrind, perl) - runs
#              where present
#   port       encodes GNU-internal assumptions; covered by a golden
#              port instead of the script

